{
  "slug": "singularity-claude",
  "name": "Singularity Claude",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Self-evolving skill engine for Claude Code. Creates, scores, repairs, and hardens skills autonomously through recursive improvement cycles. Includes 7 skills (create, score, repair, crystallize, review, dashboard), 2 agents (skill-assessor, gap-detector), and utility scripts. Skills are scored after every execution — low scores trigger automatic repair, high scores lead to crystallization (locked, immutable versions). No external dependencies.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills**, **2 agents** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `creating-skills` (Use when a new reusable skill needs to be built, either detected by gap analysis, requested by the…), `crystallizing` (Use when a skill has proven itself with consistently high scores across multiple executions and should be locked…), `dashboard` (Use when wanting an overview of all singularity-managed skills showing their scores, maturity levels, trends, and alerts via…), `repairing` (Use when a singularity-managed skill is failing, scoring below threshold, or producing incorrect outputs that need automated correction…), `reviewing` (Use when wanting to assess the health of a singularity-managed skill, check its maturity, decide whether it needs…), `scoring` (Use after any singularity-managed skill execution to rate performance 0-100, track quality over time, and trigger repair when…), `using-singularity` (Use when starting any conversation where skills may need to be created, evaluated, repaired, or when a capability…)\n- **Agents** (2): `gap-detector` (Analyzes a failed or unsatisfied task to determine if a new skill should be created), `skill-assessor` (Evaluates the quality of a skill execution output against the Singularity scoring rubric)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install singularity-claude@claude-community` from `Shmayro/singularity-claude`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 7,
    "agent": 2,
    "hook": 1
  },
